1946391,0.00839,0.07441936,-0.01532117,-0.05485726,0.086694,-0.10112106,0.00946206,0.0184573,-0.01784924,0.00092592,0.05217885,0.08291539,-0.04243027,0.00147069,-0.01070106,0.00857067,0.01275628,0.1972468,0.05560317,0.03573824,-0.00666147,-0.05747955,0.00338653,0.04169871,0.04705781,0.04098417,0.01411169,0.0444617,0.00699071,0.0120459,-0.04531782,-0.02543334,0.03241547,0.0298261,0.01096972,-0.01555306,0.00636106,-0.01198139,-0.05772068,0.12707229,-0.01829805,-0.02846029,-0.04635938,-0.04796492,-0.01000231,-0.00313291,-0.00455523,-0.02379112,0.02402102,0.06172012,0.03211376,0.00972331,-0.01712852,-0.0294512,-0.00669802,0.00608461,-0.00531678,0.01398826,-0.00036646,-0.03946752],"last_embed":{"tokens":446,"hash":"12jtg4h"}}},"last_read":{"hash":"12jtg4h","at":1785430525124},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785180590242,"size":25738,"at":1785430487845,"hash":"12jtg4h"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,10],"##Microsoft moved Translytical Task Flows from preview to general availability at FabCon 2026 in March. The feature lets users take action — update records, add annotations, trigger workflows — directly from inside a Power BI report, powered by Fabric User Data Functions written in Python. Most coverage of this announcement has framed it as “Power BI now supports write-back.” That framing is technically accurate and strategically incomplete. What actually changed is that Power BI is no longer just a reporting tool. It’s becoming an action layer. Here’s what the GA release actually delivers, where it fits in real workflows, the architecture choices it forces, and the operational tradeoffs the marketing leaves out.":[11,16],"##Microsoft moved Translytical Task Flows from preview to general availability at FabCon 2026 in March. The feature lets users take action — update records, add annotations, trigger workflows — directly from inside a Power BI report, powered by Fabric User Data Functions written in Python. Most coverage of this announcement has framed it as “Power BI now supports write-back.” That framing is technically accurate and strategically incomplete. What actually changed is that Power BI is no longer just a reporting tool. It’s becoming an action layer. Here’s what the GA release actually delivers, where it fits in real workflows, the architecture choices it forces, and the operational tradeoffs the marketing leaves out.#{1}":[13,16],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)":[17,45],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{1}":[19,22],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{2}":[23,23],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{3}":[24,24],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{4}":[25,25],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{5}":[26,26],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{6}":[27,27],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{7}":[28,28],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{8}":[29,30],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{9}":[31,32],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{10}":[33,33],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{11}":[34,34],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{12}":[35,35],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{13}":[36,37],"##What Actually Got Released (Verified Facts)#{14}":[38,45],"##Why This Is Bigger Than “Power BI Now Has Write-Back”":[46,65],"##Why This Is Bigger Than “Power BI Now Has Write-Back”#{1}":[48,65],"##Where Translytical Task Flows Genuinely Fit":[66,87],"##Where Translytical Task Flows Genuinely Fit#{1}":[68,87],"##The Architecture Choices It Forces":[88,105],"##The Architecture Choices It Forces#{1}":[90,105],"##What the Marketing Doesn’t Cover":[106,125],"##What the Marketing Doesn’t Cover#{1}":[108,125],"##When This Is the Right Architectural Choice":[126,145],"##When This Is the Right Architectural Choice#{1}":[128,145],"##How This Fits With the Broader Fabric AI Story":[146,172],"##How This Fits With the Broader Fabric AI Story#{1}":[148,149]